==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Base]].
*1 [[Great Angel Chibinel]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*10 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*1 [[Johnnyleon]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*5 [[J.J. Jackrabbit]]s spawn after 43.33 seconds<sup>1,300f</sup>, delay 43.33~46.67 seconds<sup>1,300f~1,400f</sup>.
*1 [[M. Ost]] spawns after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>.
*2 [[Great Angel Chibinel]]s spawn after 93.33 seconds<sup>2,800f</sup>, delay 53.33~60 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 75% HP:
**5 [[J.J. Jackrabbit]]s spawn, delay 1~2 seconds<sup>30f~60f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage isn't that bad if you have something to snipe Chibinel, like a [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance unit]]. Be sure to bring your [[:Category:Anti-Relic Cats|anti-Relic]] of preference to deal with the M. Ost. [[Courier Cat]] here is very good for Johnnyleon and J.J. Jackrabbits. One strategy is to use [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Master Uril]]'s [[Surge Attack]] to keep M. Ost behind Johnnyleon so Courier can kill both of them quickly, which would also allow [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]] to hit Johnnyleon, chipping down Chibinel in the process. You can also try to use [[Hermit Cat (Special Cat)|Hermit Cat]] to snipe Chibinel whilst keeping M. Ost under control, ideally with a steady meatshield stream so as to not lose too much ground too fast.

Alternatively, since the majority of threats in this stage spawn on a timer, you can try to rush the first Chibinel down with [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], and reliably destroy the base before M. Ost has a chance to wreak havoc.

On repeats, it would be recommended to bring [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Cat Mask Doron]], whose ability to freeze [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relics]] can keep M. Ost stalled for a couple seconds if timed correctly, opening the opportunity for your other units to deal enough damage to knock him behind the base, which can be a deciding factor towards whether or not you clear the stage.

==Trivia==
*Like all [[Bazaar of the Pirate King]] stages, Inn-Dependence Day is named after a movie, in this case ''[[:wikipedia:Independence Day (1996 film)|Independence Day]]''. The presence of [[Johnnyleon]], an [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]], may reference the alien invasion in the movie.
*Prior to [[Version 15.3 Update|Version 15.3]], the stage width was set to 4,800. The change was made because of a bug in how [[:Category:Animated Enemy Bases|Animated Bases]] spawn when not set as bosses.

